I have a complete picture. Here are my findings.

## Summary

This is a Spring PetClinic-derived codebase. All the relevant logic lives in the **owner "function" package**: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/`. Everything is date-derived off the owner's `registrationDate`, which is business-day-adjusted at build time.

---

## 1. Membership identifier (code/string with a year segment)

The "membership number" is formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, where `YY` is the last two digits of the registration-date year. It is computed in **two places** (both identical):

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** — the canonical read-model exposure (line 22):
```java
22  @Mapping(target = "membershipNumber", expression = "java(owner.getCustomerCode() == null || owner.getRegistrationDate() == null ? null : owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" + String.format(\"%02d\", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100))")
```

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`** — duplicated in the audit-log line (lines 24-29):
```java
24  private static String membershipNumber(Owner owner) {
25      if (owner.getCustomerCode() == null || owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) {
26          return null;
27      }
28      return owner.getCustomerCode() + "-M" + String.format("%02d", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100);
29  }
```

The `customerCode` base segment (the `<REGION>-<HASH8>` prefix, no year) is built in **`AssignCustomerCode.java`** (lines 18-22), with its Luhn `checkDigit` in **`CustomerCodeCheckDigit.java`**. The OpenAPI contract documents the format at `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml:2126-2128`.

## 2. Tenure calculation (elapsed years via 365-day window)

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/OwnerMembershipLevel.java`** — class `OwnerMembershipLevel`. Tenure is a 365-day-window check contributing 3 membership points (lines 31-33, 52-55):
```java
31      if (tenureDays(owner) > 365) {
32          points += 3;
33      }
...
52  private static long tenureDays(Owner owner) {
53      LocalDate registrationDate = owner.getRegistrationDate();
54      return registrationDate == null ? 0 : ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(registrationDate, LocalDate.now());
55  }
```

